3. A history of allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplantation or solid organ transplantation;
4. Positive for hepatitis B surface antigen (HBsAg) at screening with evidence of viral replication confirmed by HBV-DNA test;
5. Positive for hepatitis C virus antibody (HCV-Ab) at screening with evidence of viral replication confirmed by HCV-RNA test;
6. Positive for human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) antigen/antibody test at screening;
7. History of major surgery or severe trauma within 28 days prior to the first administration of the study drug;
8. Presence of severe cardiovascular disease.;
9. Persistent alcohol or drug abuse;
10. Inability to take oral medication, or presence of severe gastrointestinal dysfunctional diseases, or history of surgery with severe impact on gastrointestinal function.
11. Pregnant or lactating females.
12. Concurrent participation in other interventional clinical trials, or an interval of less than 1 month between the signing date of the informed consent form and the last administration of the study drug in the previous clinical trial;

